{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>Remember them</b> — to give you their reward, upon those defiled from the priesthood and defiled from the covenant of the priesthood, and the Levites, in taking foreign women." "<b>Defiled ones of the priesthood</b> — a descriptive noun on the pattern of תאמי צביה, and they are like פעולים in meaning, only because of the alef, which is a guttural letter, they vocalized it [with pataḥ], thus to expand its reading, and the meaning of גאלי is like the meaning of מותרים."], :book :nehemiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {1 "Vocalization terms: נקדוהו 'they vocalized it' refers to the pataḥ under the gimel in גאלי, which Ibn Ezra explains as necessitated by the guttural alef; מקראו may refer to the lemma or to the word's pronunciation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nehemiah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nechemya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:15:45.031547451Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}